    exponent is modified from the superfluid value (β = 1.0)
    to the supersolid value (β = 0.5).
    
    The velocity profile is:
      V_vortex(R) = V_flat × (1 - exp(-(R/r_t)^β))
    
    Parameters
    ----------
    R : array_like
        Radii (kpc)
    V_flat : float
        Flat rotation velocity (km/s)
    beta : float
        Vortex core exponent (default 0.5 for supersolid)
    
    Returns
    -------
    V_vortex : array_like
        Vortex contribution to rotation velocity (km/s)
    """
    a_base = 3700.0  # km²/s²/kpc — lattice acceleration
    
    # Transition radius from V_flat and lattice acceleration
    r_t = V_flat**2 / a_base
    
    # Vortex wake profile
    V_vortex = V_flat * (1.0 - np.exp(-(np.asarray(R) / r_t)**beta))
    
    return V_vortex

