    where σ is the surface tension and A is the droplet area.
    
    The mass is DEFINED as:
      m = E_rest / c²
    
    where c² is the lattice sound speed squared.
    
    Therefore:
      E = mc²
    
    This is not an empirical relation. It is the definition of mass
    in a medium where rest energy is phase boundary energy.
    
